+++ b/README.md
@@ -56,6 +56,17 @@
 The private `.env` contains only the TypeSafe key, Codex binary and model names.
 The installed `jev-computer-use` skill supplies preview, inspection and bounded
 live launchers. Upstream cost and latency claims below do not measure this adapter.
+The installed launcher defaults to full-display Korean/English OCR; set
+`CLICKER_FULL_SCREEN=0` for window cropping or `CLICKER_OCR_LANGUAGES` for another
+supported language list. Retina OCR normalizes to 1920 pixels and restores click
+coordinates. Answers always retain `answer-raw.png` and `answer-evidence.json`;
+`goal_achieved` is a model judgment and `verification_required` remains true.
+For a named app, use `--target-app` and optionally an observed `--window-id` or
+`--window-title`. The window is captured independently of foreground focus and pinned
+for that run. AX controls are used in the background. Native fallback input temporarily
+activates and validates the target, then restores the previous app; `--background-only`
+refuses that fallback. Locked sessions stop input. This behavior is tested on a small
+AppKit fixture and a Chrome permission dialog, not every native application.

 macOS 14 or newer, Python 3.12 or newer, [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/).

